
3
00:01:03,772 --> 00:01:05,904
911. What's your emergency?

4
00:01:06,865 --> 00:01:08,026
Hello?

5
00:01:10,199 --> 00:01:12,161
This is 911. Go ahead.

6
00:01:13,322 --> 00:01:16,785
This is Suh Young-chul, who used to work at Chains Bio.

7
00:01:17,626 --> 00:01:21,920
Today at the Doongwoori Building I plan to run an experiment.

8
00:01:22,291 --> 00:01:25,003
Excuse me? Can you repeat that, please?

9
00:01:25,043 --> 00:01:27,336
Ah, not an experiment.

10
00:01:27,636 --> 00:01:29,047
It's closer to terrorism.

11
00:01:29,218 --> 00:01:30,049
What?

12
00:01:30,179 --> 00:01:35,054
That's right. A highly contagious bio terror attack.

13
00:01:38,727 --> 00:01:41,560
I tested the pathogen in my body.

14
00:01:48,107 --> 00:01:50,069
And it was a success.

15
00:01:51,490 --> 00:01:55,614
I am the only vaccine that can stop this outbreak.

16
00:01:59,078 --> 00:02:01,080
Organisms of the same species that,

17
00:02:01,120 --> 00:02:03,332
for a certain time, live in the same place.

18
00:02:17,636 --> 00:02:19,228
Why are you waiting for me?

19
00:02:20,689 --> 00:02:23,392
You're 10 minutes late. What was it this time?

20
00:02:24,393 --> 00:02:25,694
It was nothing.

21
00:02:25,814 --> 00:02:26,565
Traffic was bad,

22
00:02:26,645 --> 00:02:28,987
so the taxi driver tried to let me off across the street.

23
00:02:29,448 --> 00:02:30,448
So?

24
00:02:31,029 --> 00:02:33,152
Yeah, these things happen.

25
00:02:34,032 --> 00:02:37,286
It's okay if I say it, but how can he say that to me?

26
00:02:37,326 --> 00:02:38,407
So?

27
00:02:40,539 --> 00:02:41,960
It's not what I wanted.

28
00:02:42,211 --> 00:02:43,912
I said, however long it takes,

29
00:02:43,962 --> 00:02:45,834
drop me off at the spot I chose.

30
00:02:50,419 --> 00:02:51,419
What?

31
00:02:52,171 --> 00:02:54,012
So it's my fault again?

32
00:02:54,263 --> 00:02:56,361
Welcome to the Chains Blo Conference,

33
00:02:56,385 --> 00:02:58,807
a leading platform for future technology.

34
00:02:58,847 --> 00:02:59,888
Thank you.

35
00:03:00,349 --> 00:03:02,271
You brought the invitation I gave you?

36
00:03:02,731 --> 00:03:05,684
And now we'll hear from CEO Kang Woo-cheol.

37
00:03:05,734 --> 00:03:07,566
Please give him a round of applause.

38
00:03:13,652 --> 00:03:14,510
Is that the guy?

39
00:03:14,534 --> 00:03:17,156
The one I should grovel to if I want to work here?

40
00:03:18,327 --> 00:03:20,925
If only you got along with your dean,

41
00:03:20,949 --> 00:03:22,951
this wouldn't be necessary.

42
00:03:23,912 --> 00:03:26,335
Sure, my fault again.

43
00:03:27,256 --> 00:03:28,983
But don't you care how that dean

44
00:03:29,007 --> 00:03:30,645
treated his graduate students?

45
00:03:30,669 --> 00:03:32,091
No, I don't.

46
00:03:32,511 --> 00:03:34,963
Well, I'm sure he's a jerk.

47
00:03:35,214 --> 00:03:37,096
And you couldn't tolerate that.

48
00:03:37,766 --> 00:03:40,179
So you got on his bad side, and didn't get reappointed.

49
00:03:43,021 --> 00:03:45,023
I'm just curious...

50
00:03:45,524 --> 00:03:47,792
Why are you so fixated on your ex-wife's career

51
00:03:47,816 --> 00:03:49,188
10 years after the divorce?

52
00:03:50,979 --> 00:03:52,651
Because you have no friends.

53
00:03:53,402 --> 00:03:56,261
You keep doing things that make people hate you.

54
00:03:56,285 --> 00:03:58,713
Does your wife know you look after your ex-wife like this?

55
00:03:58,737 --> 00:04:02,291
My wife is not as sensitive as you are.

56
00:04:02,791 --> 00:04:04,873
She's probably even concerned for you.

57
00:04:05,584 --> 00:04:06,835
What a cool wife.

58
00:04:07,416 --> 00:04:10,169
You're a great match. I'm happy for you.

59
00:04:10,339 --> 00:04:12,897
If I say our company's main business

60
00:04:12,921 --> 00:04:14,899
is collective intelligence,

61
00:04:14,923 --> 00:04:16,425
people might wonder,

62
00:04:16,555 --> 00:04:17,942
"Why is a bio company,

63
00:04:17,966 --> 00:04:21,140
rather than an IT company, studying that topic?"

64
00:04:21,640 --> 00:04:24,289
Collective intelligence is a common term

65
00:04:24,313 --> 00:04:26,145
in the field of sociology,

66
00:04:26,315 --> 00:04:29,318
but the first person to use the term

67
00:04:29,478 --> 00:04:32,321
was an entomologist who studied ants,

68
00:04:32,361 --> 00:04:34,193
William Morton Wheeler.

69
00:04:34,483 --> 00:04:37,736
Collective intelligence is a key force driving evolution.

70
00:04:38,077 --> 00:04:41,240
You know the yellow slime mold 'Physarum polycephalum'?

71
00:04:41,660 --> 00:04:43,308
These fellows upgrade themselves

72
00:04:43,332 --> 00:04:44,809
through information exchange

73
00:04:44,833 --> 00:04:48,036
and optimize the direction of their growth towards food.

74
00:04:48,537 --> 00:04:50,515
Although not multicellular organisms,

75
00:04:50,539 --> 00:04:52,131
they can learn and remember.

76
00:04:52,591 --> 00:04:55,110
Inspired by these remarkable traits,

77
00:04:55,134 --> 00:04:56,885
we were able to dramatically improve

78
00:04:56,925 --> 00:04:58,967
the production of organic semiconductors.

79
00:04:59,388 --> 00:05:01,970
Let's give a hand to our little collaborators.

80
00:05:06,014 --> 00:05:08,517
This guy's more interesting than I expected.

81
00:05:08,767 --> 00:05:11,610
This isn't some lame company that makes copycat drugs.

82
00:05:11,730 --> 00:05:13,732
It's a serious, enterprising firm.

83
00:05:14,063 --> 00:05:15,540
After I introduced you,

84
00:05:15,564 --> 00:05:17,776
they even sent another invitation for you.

85
00:05:18,777 --> 00:05:20,909
Actually, that's why I came.

86
00:05:21,490 --> 00:05:24,203
I was curious what this message meant.

87
00:05:24,373 --> 00:05:26,285
To Prof. Kwon: Imperfect communication,

88
00:05:26,325 --> 00:05:27,576
the source of all tragedy

89
00:05:27,626 --> 00:05:30,919
so this chip helps damaged nerves carry information.

90
00:05:31,080 --> 00:05:34,673
We injected it into a rat with severed spinal nerves

91
00:05:34,713 --> 00:05:36,465
and paralyzed hind legs,

92
00:05:37,045 --> 00:05:40,259
and as you can see, just a moment later,

93
00:05:40,719 --> 00:05:43,892
It was able to move no different from a healthy rat.

94
00:05:51,150 --> 00:05:53,128
If we continue with this research,

95
00:05:53,152 --> 00:05:55,484
and apply it to the human brain,

96
00:05:55,694 --> 00:05:58,817
I believe it may enable a direct transfer

97
00:05:58,857 --> 00:06:01,610
of information between individuals.

98
00:06:02,701 --> 00:06:04,032
When that happens,

99
00:06:04,413 --> 00:06:06,205
we may live in a world where

100
00:06:06,245 --> 00:06:09,418
you can't think bad thoughts in front of others.

101
00:06:10,959 --> 00:06:12,831
Thank you, CEO Kang.

102
00:06:13,001 --> 00:06:15,464
Please give him a round of applause!

103
00:06:23,011 --> 00:06:25,434
Next, to introduce Chains Bio's global market strategy...

104
00:06:32,771 --> 00:06:34,733
It's your first vacation in ages.

105
00:06:35,064 --> 00:06:38,607
So why spend it with the younger brother you see every day?

106
00:06:38,697 --> 00:06:42,927
This way I can get some fresh air, go shopping...

107
00:06:42,951 --> 00:06:45,364
You know how stifling it is working at a computer all day?

108
00:06:50,369 --> 00:06:54,002
Wow, look at all the camping stuff they have these days.

109
00:06:54,213 --> 00:06:55,794
I could just live outdoors.

110
00:06:57,045 --> 00:06:58,507
The clothes are nice, too.

111
00:07:00,509 --> 00:07:02,801
Should we go camping? On your next vacation?

112
00:07:03,472 --> 00:07:05,884
-The two of us? - Yeah, let's go.

113
00:07:06,175 --> 00:07:07,516
We'll grill some meat...

114
00:07:07,596 --> 00:07:09,268
That'd be great!

115
00:07:09,768 --> 00:07:11,366
We can go, why not?

116
00:07:11,390 --> 00:07:13,982
That's great. I'll buy some equipment. SECURITY.

117
00:07:14,733 --> 00:07:17,082
You get back to work. Lunchtime will end soon.

118
00:07:17,106 --> 00:07:19,914
- No, I'll head back after you. - No need.

119
00:07:19,938 --> 00:07:22,651
The facilities here are great. So convenient.

120
00:07:23,362 --> 00:07:27,802
Don't I work my ass off so I can live in civilization?

121
00:07:27,826 --> 00:07:30,055
You always go on about civilization,

122
00:07:30,079 --> 00:07:31,976
why do you want to go camping?

123
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:33,662
Camping is civilization, too.

124
00:07:33,872 --> 00:07:35,794
Go on. See you at home.

125
00:07:36,085 --> 00:07:37,626
I'll look around before going.

126
00:07:39,047 --> 00:07:39,644
Selamat tinggal.

127
00:07:39,668 --> 00:07:40,668
-Take care..- Yeah.

128
00:07:41,170 --> 00:07:42,170
Take care. Yeah.

129
00:07:45,134 --> 00:07:47,926
Hello, sir. I enjoyed your presentation.

130
00:07:48,057 --> 00:07:49,638
Oh, Professor Han.

131
00:07:49,848 --> 00:07:53,222
This is Professor Kwon Se-jeong, who I mentioned last time.

132
00:07:53,472 --> 00:07:55,023
Thank you for inviting me.

133
00:07:55,064 --> 00:07:57,646
And for this note on my invitation.

134
00:07:58,607 --> 00:07:59,858
Just a moment.

135
00:08:00,729 --> 00:08:01,780
Hello?

136
00:08:01,940 --> 00:08:03,031
Mr. Kang Woo-cheol?

137
00:08:03,532 --> 00:08:05,284
Yes. Who's speaking?

138
00:08:05,324 --> 00:08:08,077
I'm Lee Bong-seok, from the Seoul Counterterrorism Squad.

139
00:08:08,197 --> 00:08:09,488
How can I help you?

140
00:08:09,658 --> 00:08:11,370
You know a man named Suh Young-chul?

141
00:08:12,121 --> 00:08:14,769
This call seems important. Let's talk later.

142
00:08:14,793 --> 00:08:16,875
Ah, sure. We'll wait.

143
00:08:20,419 --> 00:08:22,551
You sure he's the one who sent this invitation?

144
00:08:22,591 --> 00:08:24,383
What are you doing? Go after him.

145
00:08:24,593 --> 00:08:25,071
What?

146
00:08:25,095 --> 00:08:26,885
Just hand him your card

147
00:08:26,925 --> 00:08:30,179
and say "I'm Kwon Se-jeong," that's all.,

148
00:08:38,437 --> 00:08:40,649
Why are you looking for Dr. Suh?

149
00:08:40,899 --> 00:08:41,876
We received a call

150
00:08:41,900 --> 00:08:44,169
that Dr. Suh is planning a terrorist attack

151
00:08:44,193 --> 00:08:46,405
in the building hosting your conference.

152
00:08:49,078 --> 00:08:51,080
I think I saw him today at the conference.

153
00:08:51,240 --> 00:08:52,241
Are you certain?

154
00:08:52,951 --> 00:08:54,333
Not 100% certain.

155
00:08:54,583 --> 00:08:56,085
He was standing too far away.

156
00:08:56,285 --> 00:08:58,643
Our team will arrive there soon.

157
00:08:58,667 --> 00:09:00,895
If you see him again, call me immediately at this number.

158
00:09:00,919 --> 00:09:02,291
All right, I will.

159
00:09:28,067 --> 00:09:29,738
Nice speech, Woo-cheol.

160
00:09:30,159 --> 00:09:31,450
So impressive.

161
00:09:32,321 --> 00:09:34,453
Information exchange through organic semiconductors?

162
00:09:35,284 --> 00:09:39,208
You know how hard I researched that.

163
00:09:40,329 --> 00:09:42,711
Consciousness in a multilateral network.

164
00:09:43,292 --> 00:09:46,135
Well, if that existed,

165
00:09:46,715 --> 00:09:49,758
no one would be betrayed and kicked out like me, right?

166
00:09:50,219 --> 00:09:51,470
You freak.

167
00:09:52,841 --> 00:09:56,185
The technology you researched can't be used anywhere.

168
00:09:57,686 --> 00:09:58,686
Bro.

169
00:09:59,308 --> 00:10:02,601
I'm taking humanity to the next level.

170
00:10:04,063 --> 00:10:06,565
Enabling a second cognitive revolution.

171
00:10:11,780 --> 00:10:12,951
You know what?

172
00:10:13,492 --> 00:10:14,663
You...

173
00:10:15,864 --> 00:10:17,616
are just a psycho.

174
00:10:18,167 --> 00:10:20,249
Get lost, you loser!

175
00:10:25,334 --> 00:10:27,126
But when you hired me,

176
00:10:27,586 --> 00:10:29,968
you said my research was great.

177
00:10:30,129 --> 00:10:32,221
That you respected my research.

178
00:10:33,262 --> 00:10:37,346
It was all just an act, so you could steal my research.

179
00:10:38,347 --> 00:10:40,099
And now... psycho?

180
00:10:40,939 --> 00:10:43,272
You stole research from that psycho.

181
00:10:44,643 --> 00:10:48,567
You just want to make humans go extinct, don't you?

182
00:10:49,528 --> 00:10:51,200
Not extinct.

183
00:10:51,320 --> 00:10:52,651
It's a birth.

184
00:10:53,072 --> 00:10:54,653
The birth of a new humanity.

185
00:10:55,074 --> 00:10:56,615
Just imagine it.

186
00:10:56,825 --> 00:10:59,288
Perfect communication will be possible.

187
00:10:59,578 --> 00:11:02,121
All the byproducts of crass individualism,

188
00:11:02,161 --> 00:11:04,123
jealousy, rivalry, suspicion...

189
00:11:05,794 --> 00:11:09,338
Those bizarre losses that arise from unstable communication.

190
00:11:09,668 --> 00:11:11,550
That's what I'm trying to stop.

191
00:11:15,054 --> 00:11:16,095
Wow!

192
00:11:19,428 --> 00:11:21,480
You crazy freak.

193
00:11:23,232 --> 00:11:24,313
Give it a try.

194
00:11:24,603 --> 00:11:26,024
It's got nothing to do with me.

195
00:11:26,435 --> 00:11:29,108
I'm clocking out, so good luck with that.

196
00:11:30,899 --> 00:11:35,284
I want you to be the link between me and the new humanity.

197
00:11:42,201 --> 00:11:43,321
What the hell are you doing?

198
00:11:43,622 --> 00:11:44,583
Research.

199
00:11:44,623 --> 00:11:45,954
You goddamned maniac!

200
00:12:27,916 --> 00:12:29,128
Hey, look at this.

201
00:12:29,588 --> 00:12:30,629
Hey mister!

202
00:12:30,709 --> 00:12:32,211
Shouldn't we call 911?

203
00:12:51,400 --> 00:12:52,401
Did you talk to him?

204
00:12:55,023 --> 00:12:56,341
Seemed like a bad time.

205
00:12:56,365 --> 00:12:58,367
Really? Just a sec.

206
00:13:00,449 --> 00:13:03,202
No, really. I don't think he'll want to talk now.

207
00:13:09,748 --> 00:13:12,211
Let's go eat. He'll call back.

208
00:13:24,853 --> 00:13:27,015
Police. Where's the conference hall?

209
00:13:27,146 --> 00:13:29,648
Turn left and go up the stairs, then...

210
00:13:34,653 --> 00:13:35,653
What is that?

211
00:13:39,618 --> 00:13:40,618
Go.

212
00:13:41,660 --> 00:13:43,162
Sir, are you okay?

213
00:13:49,248 --> 00:13:50,605
Call the containment team. - What?

214
00:13:50,629 --> 00:13:51,960
Call for a lockdown!

215
00:14:00,969 --> 00:14:01,617
Hi!

216
00:14:01,641 --> 00:14:04,143
Where are you, Daddy? What are you doing?

217
00:14:04,303 --> 00:14:05,974
I'll head home now.

218
00:14:06,095 --> 00:14:08,437
Honey, where's your passport?

219
00:14:08,557 --> 00:14:10,809
Should be in the drawer in the study.

220
00:14:11,940 --> 00:14:14,459
- You still with Professor Kwon? - Yeah.

221
00:14:14,483 --> 00:14:15,944
I'll head home soon.

222
00:14:16,445 --> 00:14:17,446
Want to say hi?

223
00:14:20,989 --> 00:14:22,911
Anyway, hurry home. We need to pack.

224
00:14:23,072 --> 00:14:23,759
Okay.

225
00:14:23,783 --> 00:14:26,415
Say bye to Dad. - Hurry home, Dad!

226
00:14:27,826 --> 00:14:29,328
Where are you going? Traveling?

227
00:14:33,422 --> 00:14:36,085
Why don't you answer? You immigrating or something?

228
00:14:36,625 --> 00:14:38,006
Well...

229
00:14:38,547 --> 00:14:41,090
A teaching position opened at UC Irvine...

230
00:14:41,340 --> 00:14:44,383
Really, you're going to the US? For how long?

231
00:14:45,134 --> 00:14:47,766
This time, we may just stay there.

232
00:14:54,733 --> 00:14:57,356
Ah, now I get it.

233
00:14:57,986 --> 00:15:00,028
You're leaving, so you wanted to set

234
00:15:00,069 --> 00:15:02,401
your ex-wife up with a job before going?

235
00:15:03,362 --> 00:15:04,613
Anyway, congrats.

236
00:15:04,743 --> 00:15:06,365
It's good news, right?

237
00:15:09,618 --> 00:15:12,040
Since it's the last time, let me ask.

238
00:15:13,332 --> 00:15:15,294
Why did you marry me?

239
00:15:18,877 --> 00:15:20,469
Well...

240
00:15:21,340 --> 00:15:24,859
The way you never back down when you think you're right...

241
00:15:24,883 --> 00:15:26,515
your personality?

242
00:15:26,675 --> 00:15:30,229
Wow, after you always begged me not to do that.

243
00:15:30,479 --> 00:15:31,850
You liked that?

244
00:15:33,272 --> 00:15:36,065
I did... I liked it.

245
00:15:37,066 --> 00:15:38,817
But I couldn't keep up with you.

246
00:15:39,188 --> 00:15:41,240
I couldn't handle it.

247
00:15:41,690 --> 00:15:44,443
I've always been a bit of a coward.

248
00:15:45,864 --> 00:15:48,077
That's why I broke up with you.

249
00:15:51,750 --> 00:15:54,453
Don't worry. I'll be okay.

250
00:15:55,584 --> 00:15:58,207
It's not like you, talking like that.

251
00:15:59,258 --> 00:16:00,565
I'm not saying you should change...

252
00:16:00,589 --> 00:16:01,670
Done eating?

253
00:16:02,010 --> 00:16:04,463
Let's go, your wife is waiting.

254
00:16:05,264 --> 00:16:06,925
There she goes again...

255
00:16:11,470 --> 00:16:12,471
Thank you.

256
00:16:14,273 --> 00:16:15,894
Have a good evening.

257
00:16:17,646 --> 00:16:18,897
Welcome.

258
00:16:19,108 --> 00:16:20,859
Shit, that's so funny. Yeah...

259
00:16:22,281 --> 00:16:23,822
Hey, I'll call you back.

260
00:16:24,032 --> 00:16:25,734
I'm gonna stuff my face.

261
00:16:26,155 --> 00:16:27,155
Yeah.

262
00:16:29,408 --> 00:16:31,200
Three people? - Yes, three.

263
00:16:31,370 --> 00:16:35,164
From here to here... we'll take it all.

264
00:16:35,664 --> 00:16:36,295
All of it?

265
00:16:36,665 --> 00:16:37,876
Yeah, all of it.

266
00:16:43,172 --> 00:16:45,174
You're paying today.

267
00:16:46,215 --> 00:16:47,215
Faham Got it?

268
00:16:50,429 --> 00:16:52,351
Damn it, So-eun!

269
00:16:53,182 --> 00:16:55,394
You should answer him, huh?

270
00:16:59,648 --> 00:17:01,770
The entire building is being locked down.

271
00:17:01,940 --> 00:17:04,653
Security personnel, evacuate everyone immediately!

272
00:17:05,984 --> 00:17:06,984
What's going on?

273
00:17:10,529 --> 00:17:11,529
Hey!

274
00:17:19,748 --> 00:17:20,539
Everyone evacuate!

275
00:17:20,589 --> 00:17:22,251
Move! Out of the way!

276
00:17:25,594 --> 00:17:28,637
Come out! Everyone move!

277
00:17:37,226 --> 00:17:39,308
Isn't the parking lot that way?

278
00:17:39,438 --> 00:17:40,519
Se-jeong.

279
00:17:42,481 --> 00:17:46,405
You should find at least one friend you can rely on.

280
00:17:51,990 --> 00:17:52,990
Everyone run!

281
00:17:53,372 --> 00:17:54,413
Run!

282
00:18:14,012 --> 00:18:15,054
Se-jeong!

283
00:18:15,514 --> 00:18:16,555
Damn it...

284
00:18:30,659 --> 00:18:31,659
Hurry!

285
00:18:58,637 --> 00:18:59,637
That way!

286
00:19:09,698 --> 00:19:10,989
Come quick! Hurry!

287
00:19:35,554 --> 00:19:37,806
Hyun-hee, are you hurt?

288
00:19:38,517 --> 00:19:40,309
I'm okay.

289
00:19:42,681 --> 00:19:44,273
What's going on?

290
00:19:45,734 --> 00:19:47,106
It's a terrorist attack.

291
00:19:47,986 --> 00:19:49,278
Who are you?

292
00:19:49,608 --> 00:19:50,819
I'm a policeman.

293
00:19:51,110 --> 00:19:53,088
We got a call that a bio terrorist attack

294
00:19:53,112 --> 00:19:54,903
would take place in this building.

295
00:19:55,194 --> 00:19:57,826
Those people seem to have been affected by the attack.

296
00:19:57,866 --> 00:19:59,288
What the hell?

297
00:20:25,394 --> 00:20:26,435
What the fuck?

298
00:20:48,707 --> 00:20:49,838
What the hell is this?

299
00:21:19,988 --> 00:21:22,121
What are those freaks doing?

300
00:21:27,996 --> 00:21:29,878
Turn off the light.

301
00:22:11,880 --> 00:22:13,672
What about those students?

302
00:22:13,832 --> 00:22:15,544
Do something, you're a policeman!

303
00:22:15,634 --> 00:22:17,086
We're not safe here, either.

304
00:22:17,136 --> 00:22:18,733
Let's just wait for backup.

305
00:22:18,757 --> 00:22:20,339
So we're going to stand here

306
00:22:20,389 --> 00:22:22,551
and watch as those people get killed?

307
00:22:23,932 --> 00:22:24,973
Hyun-seok...

308
00:22:28,937 --> 00:22:32,441
It looks like they're going towards that sign.

309
00:22:32,731 --> 00:22:34,233
Huh? The sign?

310
00:22:41,660 --> 00:22:43,112
We can lure them with these.

311
00:22:44,203 --> 00:22:45,203
Those?

312
00:22:45,574 --> 00:22:47,326
What will you do with them?

313
00:22:48,457 --> 00:22:50,209
Use this, my wheelchair!

314
00:22:50,249 --> 00:22:52,847
What are you talking about?

315
00:22:52,871 --> 00:22:55,084
What'll you do without it?

316
00:22:55,254 --> 00:22:56,465
Didn't you see earlier?

317
00:22:56,925 --> 00:23:00,008
If I'm going to get out, I won't be able to do it on this.

318
00:23:01,470 --> 00:23:03,972
We can't just let those people die.

319
00:23:13,892 --> 00:23:15,354
Fuck!

320
00:23:44,763 --> 00:23:45,763
Hurry!

321
00:23:47,266 --> 00:23:48,204
What?

322
00:23:48,228 --> 00:23:49,678
I can't. There's no way.

323
00:23:52,601 --> 00:23:54,143
Hey, don't go out there!

324
00:24:00,859 --> 00:24:01,859
This way!

325
00:24:02,991 --> 00:24:04,032
Hurry!

326
00:24:14,083 --> 00:24:15,294
Shut up, will you?

327
00:24:15,374 --> 00:24:16,374
Hurry!

328
00:24:30,889 --> 00:24:31,930
Why'd she do that?

329
00:24:33,142 --> 00:24:34,433
I'll go get her.

330
00:24:47,696 --> 00:24:49,118
Come, let's go.

331
00:24:49,488 --> 00:24:50,765
Come with me.

332
00:24:50,789 --> 00:24:53,492
You can do it. Let's go.

333
00:24:53,702 --> 00:24:55,744
Take my hand and go.

334
00:24:56,085 --> 00:24:57,996
Let's go, hurry.

335
00:25:03,052 --> 00:25:04,053
Kyu-seong!

336
00:25:15,514 --> 00:25:17,516
Come here, asshole!

337
00:25:20,479 --> 00:25:22,361
Get in, hurry!

338
00:26:19,828 --> 00:26:21,710
If I say our company's main business

339
00:26:21,750 --> 00:26:23,382
is collective intelligence...

340
00:26:23,462 --> 00:26:24,883
"Why is a bio company,

341
00:26:24,923 --> 00:26:28,087
rather than an IT company, studying that topic?"

342
00:26:28,587 --> 00:26:30,259
These fellows upgrade themselves

343
00:26:30,299 --> 00:26:31,890
through information exchange.

344
00:26:35,224 --> 00:26:38,147
Collective intelligence is a key force driving evolution.

345
00:27:18,767 --> 00:27:19,938
Kyu-seong!

346
00:27:20,599 --> 00:27:21,730
Hurry!

347
00:27:25,274 --> 00:27:26,355
No!

348
00:28:05,484 --> 00:28:08,123
This afternoon, the Doongwoori Building

349
00:28:08,147 --> 00:28:11,820
was locked down following an act of bio-terrorism.

350
00:28:12,071 --> 00:28:15,364
Health authorities designated the location a terrorism zone,

351
00:28:15,494 --> 00:28:18,173
and a full quarantine is in effect until an investigation...

352
00:28:18,197 --> 00:28:19,828
The Counterterrorism HQ says

353
00:28:19,868 --> 00:28:22,411
the virus in question is highly contagious

354
00:28:22,621 --> 00:28:24,543
and spreads extremely quickly.

355
00:28:24,623 --> 00:28:27,416
The Disease Control Agency is devoting all its resources

356
00:28:27,506 --> 00:28:28,483
to obtaining

357
00:28:28,507 --> 00:28:29,814
and researching possible vaccines.

358
00:28:29,838 --> 00:28:31,170
Meanwhile, unconfirmed rumors

359
00:28:31,260 --> 00:28:32,711
about this bio-terrorism attack

360
00:28:32,761 --> 00:28:35,174
are rapidly spreading online.

361
00:28:35,384 --> 00:28:36,901
SWAT deployment complete.

362
00:28:36,925 --> 00:28:38,927
Double barricade of Doongwoori Building in place.

363
00:28:39,098 --> 00:28:40,309
Visual confirmation.

364
00:28:54,403 --> 00:28:56,235
Hello, shoppers.

365
00:28:56,575 --> 00:29:00,539
Thank you for visiting Doongwoori Shopping Mall today.

366
00:29:01,330 --> 00:29:04,453
The shopping mall is now closing.

367
00:29:05,204 --> 00:29:08,497
We look forward to welcoming you tomorrow

368
00:29:08,547 --> 00:29:10,629
with even better service.

369
00:29:11,420 --> 00:29:15,504
We wish you a comfortable and safe trip home.

370
00:29:15,754 --> 00:29:16,532
Thank you.

371
00:29:16,556 --> 00:29:18,677
Shit, the data's not working.

372
00:29:19,138 --> 00:29:20,759
I'm okay. Yeah.

373
00:29:22,101 --> 00:29:23,392
And you, Dad?

374
00:29:24,433 --> 00:29:26,355
My Dearest Daughter.

375
00:29:27,066 --> 00:29:28,647
Really? Thank God...

376
00:29:33,942 --> 00:29:35,154
Dad!

377
00:29:36,525 --> 00:29:38,907
- Who are you? Where's my dad? - Did Dad answer?

378
00:29:40,329 --> 00:29:41,870
Ji-hye, go to Grandma for a sec.

379
00:29:42,281 --> 00:29:43,872
- Why? - Just for a sec.

380
00:29:43,952 --> 00:29:45,100
Mom, take her.

381
00:29:45,124 --> 00:29:47,126
Right, come with me for a minute.

382
00:29:53,382 --> 00:29:54,543
What...

383
00:29:56,925 --> 00:29:58,637
What about Kyu-seong?

384
00:30:02,221 --> 00:30:03,892
Did he go somewhere?

385
00:30:06,355 --> 00:30:07,686
Kyu-seong...

386
00:30:09,228 --> 00:30:12,231
saved some people, and then...

387
00:30:13,112 --> 00:30:14,273
Who...

388
00:30:14,863 --> 00:30:16,365
Who did he save?

389
00:30:16,815 --> 00:30:18,697
Everything just sucks!

390
00:30:19,027 --> 00:30:20,279
And then what?

391
00:30:20,909 --> 00:30:23,532
And then what happened?

392
00:30:31,130 --> 00:30:32,881
-Kyu-seong... - Dad!

393
00:30:41,009 --> 00:30:42,341
What are you talking about?

394
00:30:42,931 --> 00:30:45,304
You know how long I've been stuck here?

395
00:30:47,346 --> 00:30:50,059
You won't get infected unless you're bitten!

396
00:30:51,100 --> 00:30:52,271
What did you say?

397
00:30:55,654 --> 00:30:56,695
What's this?

398
00:30:56,985 --> 00:30:58,317
What do you think?

399
00:31:01,029 --> 00:31:02,361
You're going to carry me?

400
00:31:02,531 --> 00:31:04,163
Who else is going to carry you?

401
00:31:04,913 --> 00:31:06,705
Think of it as going camping.

402
00:31:07,035 --> 00:31:11,580
This is why you should think twice before helping others.

403
00:31:14,543 --> 00:31:16,004
Listen, Officer!

404
00:31:16,125 --> 00:31:18,467
There's a rescue team coming to get us, right?

405
00:31:20,629 --> 00:31:21,630
The rescue team

406
00:31:23,382 --> 00:31:24,593
can't come in here.

407
00:31:24,723 --> 00:31:25,723
What?

408
00:31:26,014 --> 00:31:27,452
What are you saying?

409
00:31:27,476 --> 00:31:29,058
We're all still alive!

410
00:31:29,228 --> 00:31:31,560
The news has reported that this virus

411
00:31:31,600 --> 00:31:33,328
is unbelievably contagious.

412
00:31:33,352 --> 00:31:35,564
Until an epidemiological analysis is done,

413
00:31:35,604 --> 00:31:37,446
this building is under quarantine.

414
00:31:37,526 --> 00:31:38,793
Then what about us?

415
00:31:38,817 --> 00:31:41,150
They're telling us to just die here?

416
00:31:41,240 --> 00:31:42,627
I don't wanna die...

417
00:31:42,651 --> 00:31:44,743
- I don't wanna die! - I'm going fucking crazy...

418
00:31:44,823 --> 00:31:47,382
Fuck, you know how much I pay this country in taxes?

419
00:31:47,406 --> 00:31:49,708
But they won't save me?

420
00:31:50,709 --> 00:31:54,663
There is one way that we can be saved.

421
00:31:55,043 --> 00:31:56,375
What's that?

422
00:31:56,465 --> 00:31:59,298
The man behind this attack, Suh Young-chul,

423
00:31:59,338 --> 00:32:01,760
says he's injected the vaccine into his own body.

424
00:32:01,840 --> 00:32:04,803
If we find him and bring him out, we can all be rescued.

425
00:32:04,923 --> 00:32:06,305
Where is he?

426
00:32:07,096 --> 00:32:10,349
It's said he attended the seminar in this building today,

427
00:32:10,559 --> 00:32:12,731
and there's no sign that he left.

428
00:32:13,772 --> 00:32:15,234
Suh Young-chul...

429
00:32:15,774 --> 00:32:18,437
came to meet Chains Bio CEO Kang Woo-cheol.

430
00:32:19,108 --> 00:32:19,938
That's right.

431
00:32:20,069 --> 00:32:20,796
How'd you know that?

432
00:32:20,820 --> 00:32:22,071
After the seminar,

433
00:32:22,111 --> 00:32:25,404
I saw him by Kang's VIP Room on the 3rd floor.

434
00:32:25,444 --> 00:32:27,576
You must be a professor.

435
00:32:27,696 --> 00:32:29,368
Then where did he go?

436
00:32:29,408 --> 00:32:32,701
I saw him follow Kang into the room.

437
00:32:32,911 --> 00:32:34,543
So what are we supposed to do?

438
00:32:34,873 --> 00:32:36,601
We can't even set foot outside this door!

439
00:32:36,625 --> 00:32:40,209
Go up to the 3rd floor? How can we make it there?

440
00:32:40,299 --> 00:32:41,420
Right...

441
00:32:41,960 --> 00:32:43,382
Those people out there

442
00:32:43,962 --> 00:32:46,765
seem to be evolving through information exchange.

443
00:32:47,136 --> 00:32:49,017
First they walked on all fours,

444
00:32:49,218 --> 00:32:50,929
and charged at signs.

445
00:32:51,560 --> 00:32:52,931
Now they walk on two feet

446
00:32:53,642 --> 00:32:55,660
and their ability to identify humans

447
00:32:55,684 --> 00:32:57,226
is slowly taking shape.

448
00:32:57,936 --> 00:32:59,728
They're exchanging info?

449
00:32:59,858 --> 00:33:02,071
How, by calling each other?

450
00:33:02,441 --> 00:33:04,573
Words are not the only way to communicate.

451
00:33:04,983 --> 00:33:06,285
Like fungi or mushrooms,

452
00:33:06,405 --> 00:33:07,786
many creatures other than humans

453
00:33:07,866 --> 00:33:09,464
have their own communication networks.

454
00:33:09,488 --> 00:33:13,242
For example, ants communicate by pheromones.

455
00:33:13,832 --> 00:33:15,954
And to expedite the exchange of pheromones,

456
00:33:16,044 --> 00:33:18,247
they create a communication network of mucus.

457
00:33:18,377 --> 00:33:21,920
So you're saying the infected people there,

458
00:33:22,341 --> 00:33:24,343
they're in a state resembling ants?

459
00:33:24,463 --> 00:33:26,571
If they have collective intelligence based

460
00:33:26,595 --> 00:33:27,886
on information exchange,

461
00:33:28,177 --> 00:33:30,719
perhaps we can input false information.

462
00:33:32,471 --> 00:33:34,683
What, they've turned into ants?

463
00:33:34,813 --> 00:33:37,856
So how do we give them false info?

464
00:33:38,397 --> 00:33:39,768
Show them fake news?

465
00:33:39,898 --> 00:33:42,111
Ants, too, often show errant behavior

466
00:33:42,151 --> 00:33:44,193
when receiving false information.

467
00:33:44,233 --> 00:33:46,825
For example, ant mills.

468
00:33:47,616 --> 00:33:49,408
Sometimes while exchanging pheromones,

469
00:33:49,618 --> 00:33:51,240
Ant Mill an error occurs.

470
00:33:51,370 --> 00:33:54,639
At such times, they form a giant circle in one spot

471
00:33:54,663 --> 00:33:57,836
and keep turning in place, unable to stop.

472
00:33:58,747 --> 00:34:00,089
Until they die.

473
00:34:00,379 --> 00:34:03,592
So how are we going to give them false information?

474
00:34:03,962 --> 00:34:07,926
If one of us went to them giving off a special odor,

475
00:34:08,217 --> 00:34:09,984
and the rest of us stood still,

476
00:34:10,008 --> 00:34:12,351
giving off a completely different odor,

477
00:34:12,511 --> 00:34:15,054
I don't think they'd be able to recognize us as humans.

478
00:34:15,644 --> 00:34:18,107
Then until they figure out their mistake,

479
00:34:18,437 --> 00:34:20,359
we can buy ourselves some time.

480
00:34:21,650 --> 00:34:23,612
Who's gonna do that?

481
00:34:24,063 --> 00:34:25,154
I'll do it.

482
00:34:26,065 --> 00:34:27,736
You'll fail, 100%.

483
00:34:28,367 --> 00:34:31,570
Look, how about someone more fit?

484
00:34:32,201 --> 00:34:33,662
This guy should do.

485
00:34:33,822 --> 00:34:34,929
I'll do it.

486
00:34:34,953 --> 00:34:36,625
I said I'll do it.

487
00:34:37,666 --> 00:34:39,788
You're looking down on me because of my age.

488
00:34:40,129 --> 00:34:41,556
But in my 20s, I won a gold medal

489
00:34:41,580 --> 00:34:43,438
in a national track and field competition.

490
00:34:43,462 --> 00:34:44,833
Yeah sure, you stay out.

491
00:34:46,215 --> 00:34:47,216
That hurts! Ouch!

492
00:34:50,008 --> 00:34:52,091
I coached track and field before retiring.

493
00:34:52,391 --> 00:34:55,764
Professor, tell me what I should do.

494
00:35:04,773 --> 00:35:06,461
Where should I put this?

495
00:35:06,485 --> 00:35:07,656
Here.

496
00:35:07,856 --> 00:35:09,174
- Here? - Yeah.

497
00:35:09,198 --> 00:35:11,780
I added you all to a group chat, so check it.

498
00:35:12,451 --> 00:35:16,075
If they're exchanging information, we should do it, too.

499
00:35:32,931 --> 00:35:35,344
Bring back this same perfume.

500
00:35:45,444 --> 00:35:47,946
Hey, you nutjobs!

501
00:35:48,527 --> 00:35:49,818
Come and get me!

502
00:37:13,902 --> 00:37:15,033
Hurry!

503
00:37:15,404 --> 00:37:17,035
Close the door!

504
00:37:18,697 --> 00:37:20,329
I got them. Here.

505
00:37:32,841 --> 00:37:32,938
Thal antifreeze, bring it here.

506
00:37:32,962 --> 00:37:34,189
That antifreeze, bring it here!

507
00:37:34,213 --> 00:37:35,344
Antifreeze, okay!

508
00:37:40,059 --> 00:37:40,849
Here.

509
00:37:40,889 --> 00:37:41,970
That stinks!

510
00:37:42,101 --> 00:37:43,932
Why does this smell so strong?

511
00:38:04,333 --> 00:38:05,664
Ready? - Yeah.

512
00:40:15,794 --> 00:40:17,256
We can go now.

513
00:40:37,106 --> 00:40:38,106
Hurry up!

514
00:40:39,988 --> 00:40:41,190
Let's just go!

515
00:40:44,943 --> 00:40:46,075
What are you doing?

516
00:40:48,697 --> 00:40:50,539
Does anyone have a lighter?

517
00:41:20,649 --> 00:41:21,649
Hurry, run!

518
00:41:23,112 --> 00:41:24,233
Behind us!

519
00:41:45,674 --> 00:41:46,715
Run, quickly!

520
00:41:51,810 --> 00:41:52,851
Hold on tight.

521
00:42:13,202 --> 00:42:14,202
Look out!

522
00:42:52,741 --> 00:42:54,969
How did a world-renowned scientist

523
00:42:54,993 --> 00:42:57,706
become a terrorist threating the nation?

524
00:42:57,916 --> 00:43:00,919
Let's look into the background of Dr. Suh Young-chul.

525
00:43:01,039 --> 00:43:02,831
He was top-ranked at his university

526
00:43:02,881 --> 00:43:04,423
from entrance to graduation,

527
00:43:04,633 --> 00:43:07,926
and his graduation thesis "Biocomputing With Fungi"

528
00:43:08,087 --> 00:43:10,679
was published in the journal Science.

529
00:43:10,889 --> 00:43:13,280
For such a promising talent

530
00:43:13,304 --> 00:43:14,481
to suddenly commit terrorism

531
00:43:14,505 --> 00:43:15,682
and hold the nation hostage,

532
00:43:15,706 --> 00:43:17,751
it's quite hard to understand.

533
00:43:17,951 --> 00:43:18,772
Reporter Kim Seong-il,

534
00:43:18,796 --> 00:43:20,756
are there any notable details

535
00:43:20,780 --> 00:43:22,505
concerning Suh Young-chul?

536
00:43:22,705 --> 00:43:26,181
Suh's father was a professor of Applied Biology

537
00:43:26,205 --> 00:43:28,453
at Seocheong University.

538
00:43:28,477 --> 00:43:29,586
PROF. SUH DENIES MISUSE OF RESEARCH FUNDS
While he was there,

539
00:43:29,610 --> 00:43:32,391
PROF. SUH DENIES MISUSE OF RESEARCH FUNDS
an anonymous tip led to an internal report

540
00:43:32,415 --> 00:43:34,758
on misuse of funds for his research lab

541
00:43:34,782 --> 00:43:36,802
and exploitation of student researchers,

542
00:43:36,826 --> 00:43:38,756
and this was widely covered in the press.

543
00:43:38,780 --> 00:43:40,926
Four weeks after the report.

544
00:43:40,950 --> 00:43:43,604
Professor Suh chose to end his own life.

545
00:43:43,628 --> 00:43:45,880
Is there any link between this incident

546
00:43:45,904 --> 00:43:48,311
and Suh Young-chul's terrorist attack?

547
00:43:48,511 --> 00:43:51,470
Could it be some sort of revenge?

548
00:43:51,800 --> 00:43:55,224
So far, Suh has not made any requests or demands,

549
00:43:55,264 --> 00:43:58,727
so it seems unlikely that the two incidents are related.

550
00:43:58,807 --> 00:44:01,326
At the moment, the government has not released

551
00:44:01,350 --> 00:44:03,232
any information about the attack.

552
00:44:05,314 --> 00:44:06,395
3rd Floor.

553
00:44:16,655 --> 00:44:17,656
No one here.

554
00:44:17,706 --> 00:44:18,706
Hurry!

555
00:44:47,816 --> 00:44:49,438
Suh Young-chul, you are under arrest

556
00:44:49,488 --> 00:44:51,650
for the Doongwoori Building terrorist attack.

557
00:44:51,900 --> 00:44:54,469
You have the right to an attorney,

558
00:44:54,493 --> 00:44:56,325
and the right to remain silent.

559
00:44:56,575 --> 00:44:59,514
Anything you say can and will be used against you in court...

560
00:44:59,538 --> 00:45:00,659
Nice to meet you.

561
00:45:01,080 --> 00:45:04,042
Using water to disrupt their communications network,

562
00:45:04,663 --> 00:45:06,545
that was your idea, Professor Kwon?

563
00:45:06,955 --> 00:45:07,683
What's this?

564
00:45:07,707 --> 00:45:09,128
You two know each other?

565
00:45:09,228 --> 00:45:10,419
But that was a mistake.

566
00:45:12,881 --> 00:45:14,923
Water evaporates quickly.

567
00:45:15,054 --> 00:45:17,806
If water mixes in the air with their network,

568
00:45:17,846 --> 00:45:19,178
won't it work faster?

569
00:45:19,848 --> 00:45:20,848
Forget it.

570
00:45:21,470 --> 00:45:22,561
What now?

571
00:45:23,062 --> 00:45:24,313
Is the rescue team coming?

572
00:45:24,973 --> 00:45:25,973
No.

573
00:45:26,185 --> 00:45:28,413
We have to meet the rescue team on the roof.

574
00:45:28,437 --> 00:45:28,914
What?

575
00:45:28,938 --> 00:45:31,046
The rescue team must not be exposed to the infected.

576
00:45:31,070 --> 00:45:34,863
We almost died coming here, now we have to go to the roof?

577
00:45:35,033 --> 00:45:37,986
Can't the rescue team come down and wipe them all out?

578
00:45:38,697 --> 00:45:40,199
Those people are patients.

579
00:45:40,539 --> 00:45:42,741
We've been ordered not to kill them without reason.

580
00:45:42,791 --> 00:45:44,373
What bullshit!

581
00:45:44,413 --> 00:45:46,085
Those monsters out there are patients?

582
00:45:46,585 --> 00:45:48,207
Do patients kill people?

583
00:45:49,338 --> 00:45:52,211
Damn it, I don't care if they're monsters or whatever.

584
00:45:52,421 --> 00:45:55,464
At any rate, if we can get him up to the roof,

585
00:45:55,594 --> 00:45:58,597
the rescue team will come. Then we can all survive.

586
00:45:58,807 --> 00:46:01,430
We just need to find a safe way to get there.

587
00:46:02,181 --> 00:46:03,852
Is there one?

588
00:46:04,012 --> 00:46:05,013
There is.

589
00:46:05,144 --> 00:46:08,897
There's a cargo elevator that most people don't know about.

590
00:46:10,439 --> 00:46:12,521
That seems safest.

591
00:46:13,192 --> 00:46:15,274
I think that security guard's right.

592
00:46:18,277 --> 00:46:20,989
Alright, let's give it a try.

593
00:46:21,370 --> 00:46:23,122
You take the lead.

594
00:46:27,126 --> 00:46:28,417
Let's go.

595
00:46:30,379 --> 00:46:31,420
You first.

596
00:46:36,215 --> 00:46:37,296
Professor Gong!

597
00:46:41,510 --> 00:46:44,143
You got here quickly.

598
00:46:44,303 --> 00:46:45,303
Yes.

599
00:46:46,515 --> 00:46:48,373
This was Suh Young-chul's research lab?

600
00:46:48,397 --> 00:46:49,058
Yeah.

601
00:46:49,228 --> 00:46:54,153
After leaving Chains Bio, it seems he kept researching here.

602
00:46:54,523 --> 00:46:55,523
Professor Joo!

603
00:46:55,564 --> 00:46:56,564
Yeah.

604
00:46:57,116 --> 00:47:00,159
Say hello. This is Myunghan University Biotechnology.

605
00:47:00,199 --> 00:47:01,620
Professor Gong Sul-hee.

606
00:47:02,451 --> 00:47:05,009
These are professors Lee Hyeon-myeong and Jo Hyeon-mi.

607
00:47:05,033 --> 00:47:06,995
So the government has assembled

608
00:47:07,035 --> 00:47:09,054
this special investigative team.

609
00:47:09,078 --> 00:47:11,830
When the SWAT team goes in, we'll join them,

610
00:47:12,081 --> 00:47:13,688
so prepare yourself, Professor Gong.

611
00:47:13,712 --> 00:47:14,963
Understood.

612
00:47:15,714 --> 00:47:17,336
Alpha Team take the front door,

613
00:47:17,386 --> 00:47:19,088
Delta Team enter from the back.

614
00:47:36,525 --> 00:47:37,566
Shit...

615
00:47:38,237 --> 00:47:39,608
I'm gonna do it.

616
00:47:39,858 --> 00:47:41,070
I'm pushing it.

617
00:47:51,830 --> 00:47:53,172
Hurry up!

618
00:47:54,083 --> 00:47:55,294
Hurry!

619
00:47:56,295 --> 00:47:57,756
Close the door, quick!

620
00:48:03,302 --> 00:48:04,683
Going up.

621
00:48:06,975 --> 00:48:09,388
We'll be on the roof in 5 minutes.

622
00:48:12,691 --> 00:48:14,233
How old are you?

623
00:48:15,144 --> 00:48:17,066
You're in great shape for your age.

624
00:48:18,197 --> 00:48:20,149
The way you slid back there was so cool.

625
00:48:21,070 --> 00:48:22,531
You were so fast.

626
00:48:23,242 --> 00:48:24,242
Like this.

627
00:48:27,456 --> 00:48:28,456
The doors are opening.

628
00:48:46,175 --> 00:48:47,175
No!

629
00:49:11,370 --> 00:49:12,751
He got away!

630
00:49:14,203 --> 00:49:15,754
Who cares if he did?

631
00:49:16,255 --> 00:49:19,354
You really think that bastard's more important than us?

632
00:49:19,378 --> 00:49:21,090
That jerk is the vaccine.

633
00:49:21,300 --> 00:49:24,513
You saw it now. The infected didn't even touch him.

634
00:49:24,713 --> 00:49:26,595
We need to take that vaccine out with us!

635
00:49:26,715 --> 00:49:27,886
But...

636
00:49:28,467 --> 00:49:30,445
How are we supposed to bring him out?

637
00:49:30,469 --> 00:49:34,063
You saw how those monsters are swarming all over!

638
00:49:34,603 --> 00:49:37,066
How do we pull him out of there?

639
00:49:38,026 --> 00:49:39,108
The doors are opening.

640
00:49:48,867 --> 00:49:52,411
What? Are those bastards mimicking us?

641
00:49:57,876 --> 00:49:59,498
The doors are closing.

642
00:50:03,962 --> 00:50:05,504
What do we do now?

643
00:50:06,255 --> 00:50:07,506
-Hyun-seok. - Yeah?

644
00:50:07,556 --> 00:50:09,058
Is there a control room where

645
00:50:09,098 --> 00:50:10,985
you can see all the building's CCTVs?

646
00:50:11,009 --> 00:50:12,311
What? A control room?

647
00:50:12,641 --> 00:50:14,619
You should know, you're on the security team.

648
00:50:14,643 --> 00:50:15,201
Yeah.

649
00:50:15,225 --> 00:50:18,267
If we can watch all of the CCTVs,

650
00:50:18,357 --> 00:50:21,360
we can see where he's going in real time.

651
00:50:21,860 --> 00:50:23,362
The control room...

652
00:50:24,443 --> 00:50:26,301
is at the very end of Floor B2.

653
00:50:26,325 --> 00:50:27,906
B2! B2!

654
00:50:27,946 --> 00:50:30,779
For now, let's go there and look for Suh.

655
00:50:42,751 --> 00:50:44,042
Alpha, clear.

656
00:50:44,963 --> 00:50:46,295
Delta, clear.

657
00:50:47,096 --> 00:50:49,468
He's set up an entire lab here.

658
00:51:03,152 --> 00:51:04,983
You should see this over here.

659
00:51:21,170 --> 00:51:24,083
What is this? Are they all dead?

660
00:51:24,833 --> 00:51:26,135
They're alive.

661
00:51:32,971 --> 00:51:35,094
What experiment was he doing?

662
00:51:43,192 --> 00:51:45,444
Here! This one's been opened!

663
00:51:48,317 --> 00:51:49,448
Contact!

664
00:52:32,451 --> 00:52:33,742
SPECIAL OPERATION UNIT

665
00:52:40,579 --> 00:52:41,620
Attack!

666
00:52:42,291 --> 00:52:43,462
Return fire!

667
00:52:44,713 --> 00:52:45,713
Alpha down!

668
00:52:53,922 --> 00:52:55,224
Contact!

669
00:52:56,345 --> 00:52:58,307
Take her to safety!

670
00:53:36,805 --> 00:53:39,518
Targets have stopped moving. Clear, confirming.

671
00:53:39,888 --> 00:53:41,310
Clear, confirming.

672
00:53:45,974 --> 00:53:47,316
They've all stopped.

673
00:53:48,067 --> 00:53:49,528
Each defend your own zone.

674
00:53:49,568 --> 00:53:51,860
In case of danger, respond immediately.

675
00:54:39,198 --> 00:54:40,198
What's that?

676
00:54:40,449 --> 00:54:41,990
That's evolving?

677
00:54:43,242 --> 00:54:44,953
Where's the control room?

678
00:54:45,494 --> 00:54:46,535
That way.

679
00:54:46,585 --> 00:54:48,377
Okay, let's move quietly.

680
00:55:54,983 --> 00:55:56,485
Pull yourself together!

681
00:56:17,296 --> 00:56:18,507
Sit me down here.

682
00:56:18,797 --> 00:56:20,089
Close that.

683
00:56:26,305 --> 00:56:28,557
These are the main cameras.

684
00:56:29,188 --> 00:56:30,599
And for the auxiliary cams...

685
00:56:30,639 --> 00:56:31,639
CCTV.

686
00:56:33,692 --> 00:56:35,694
What floor did Suh get off on?

687
00:56:36,065 --> 00:56:37,065
8th floor?

688
00:56:37,356 --> 00:56:39,488
The 9th floor. I'll start looking there.

689
00:56:46,495 --> 00:56:48,617
You're in great shape for your age.

690
00:56:49,208 --> 00:56:51,250
The way you slid back there was so cool.

691
00:56:51,460 --> 00:56:52,911
You were so fast.

692
00:56:53,332 --> 00:56:55,294
How could Suh have known?

693
00:56:56,755 --> 00:56:58,217
The things he said in the elevator,

694
00:56:58,337 --> 00:57:00,339
as if he'd watched what we'd done.

695
00:57:02,511 --> 00:57:03,512
You're right.

696
00:57:04,423 --> 00:57:06,635
Is he watching CCTVs like us?

697
00:57:08,637 --> 00:57:12,561
If Suh can see through the eyes of the infected...

698
00:57:14,063 --> 00:57:15,104
Hold on, then...

699
00:57:16,065 --> 00:57:17,936
Whatever these monsters see,

700
00:57:18,647 --> 00:57:20,399
Suh can see the same thing?

701
00:57:20,609 --> 00:57:22,491
He sees the same thing? What the hell?

702
00:57:22,611 --> 00:57:23,612
I found him!

703
00:57:29,448 --> 00:57:31,330
Where's that bastard going?

704
00:57:55,854 --> 00:57:57,066
What's he doing?

705
00:58:01,570 --> 00:58:03,031
Where is he going?

706
00:58:05,114 --> 00:58:06,785
It seems he's searching for something.

707
00:58:07,286 --> 00:58:08,537
He stopped.

708
00:58:09,118 --> 00:58:10,489
Where is that?

709
00:58:10,829 --> 00:58:15,084
3rd Floor, Building A Hallway...

710
00:58:16,455 --> 00:58:17,586
Bro!

711
00:58:19,588 --> 00:58:22,381
You locked me up, so I had a hard time finding you.

712
00:58:28,347 --> 00:58:29,638
Oh, that's...

713
00:58:29,758 --> 00:58:31,576
CEO Kang Woo-cheol.

714
00:58:31,600 --> 00:58:32,600
Huh?

715
00:58:32,641 --> 00:58:34,723
The first person Suh met.

716
00:58:36,395 --> 00:58:39,478
He was probably the first infected.

717
00:58:46,615 --> 00:58:48,947
See, wasn't I right?

718
00:58:51,530 --> 00:58:54,743
I said you'd be my link to the new humanity.

719
00:58:55,164 --> 00:58:56,665
So hurry up and bite me.

720
00:59:08,046 --> 00:59:09,888
Wait, did he just bite him?

721
00:59:10,599 --> 00:59:11,599
What's happening to him?

722
00:59:26,065 --> 00:59:27,065
Look at them.

723
00:59:45,334 --> 00:59:47,005
I'm not sure what it is,

724
00:59:47,716 --> 00:59:49,298
but they must be receiving some

725
00:59:49,338 --> 00:59:51,180
completely new sort of information.

726
00:59:53,182 --> 00:59:57,096
What is it? Is it connected to Suh being bitten?

727
00:59:57,186 --> 00:59:58,937
I have no idea.

728
00:59:59,728 --> 01:00:02,811
Then how long will they be in this condition?

729
01:00:03,232 --> 01:00:05,040
Before, they were like that for several minutes.

730
01:00:05,064 --> 01:00:06,855
There's no way to know.

731
01:00:08,487 --> 01:00:10,199
Okay, this is our chance.

732
01:00:10,319 --> 01:00:13,112
While they're in that state, we should go get the vaccine.

733
01:00:13,532 --> 01:00:15,784
He's on the 3rd floor, it won't take long.

734
01:00:17,666 --> 01:00:20,329
I'll watch the CCTV from here

735
01:00:20,459 --> 01:00:22,961
and tell you where it's safe, through the group chat.

736
01:00:23,172 --> 01:00:25,624
What you?

737
01:00:27,796 --> 01:00:28,813
You're going to stay here?

738
01:00:28,837 --> 01:00:30,469
Get the vaccine and come back.

739
01:00:30,509 --> 01:00:32,721
Until then, I'll tell you where to go.

740
01:00:33,011 --> 01:00:34,973
How can I leave you behind?

741
01:00:35,554 --> 01:00:38,637
Listen to me. This is the safest way.

742
01:00:39,688 --> 01:00:40,849
Yes, let's do that.

743
01:00:40,939 --> 01:00:43,852
We don't know when they'll wake up, so let's hurry.

744
01:01:34,903 --> 01:01:37,406
Let's drag him to someplace safe.

745
01:01:43,372 --> 01:01:46,375
What's going on?

746
01:01:53,382 --> 01:01:54,382
Go, quick!

747
01:01:55,134 --> 01:01:56,675
Hurry! Run!

748
01:02:03,142 --> 01:02:04,603
Hurry! Get inside!

749
01:02:04,893 --> 01:02:05,934
Hurry!

750
01:02:09,978 --> 01:02:11,940
What is this freak doing?

751
01:02:14,653 --> 01:02:16,535
They're leaving.

752
01:02:47,316 --> 01:02:48,607
Go that way.

753
01:02:54,773 --> 01:02:56,024
This way, quickly!

754
01:03:17,796 --> 01:03:19,047
They're gone.

755
01:03:20,008 --> 01:03:21,680
What the hell did you do?

756
01:03:25,224 --> 01:03:28,897
Ah, did you only pretend to go out? You're smart.

757
01:03:29,808 --> 01:03:31,666
You think if you cover my eyes,

758
01:03:31,690 --> 01:03:34,153
you'll be able to get out of here alive?

759
01:03:34,233 --> 01:03:35,654
What's this freak yammering about?

760
01:03:36,565 --> 01:03:38,527
Since getting bitten by Kang Woo-cheol,

761
01:03:38,567 --> 01:03:40,659
it seems he can communicate with all of them.

762
01:03:41,070 --> 01:03:42,241
Wait, then...

763
01:03:42,701 --> 01:03:46,705
that means he can control all those monsters out there.

764
01:03:48,036 --> 01:03:50,209
Let's only communicate by texting.

765
01:03:50,249 --> 01:03:52,421
Don't let him see or hear anything.

766
01:04:06,515 --> 01:04:09,518
But didn't we file all of our reports already?

767
01:04:09,978 --> 01:04:12,191
Why are they calling us to the Counterterrorism HQ?

768
01:04:12,231 --> 01:04:14,483
We'll see when we get there.

769
01:04:39,047 --> 01:04:41,090
From office go straight to emergency exit.

770
01:04:42,010 --> 01:04:43,610
Up stairs to 4th floor, to machine room.

771
01:04:47,186 --> 01:04:48,347
Let's hurry.

772
01:05:11,540 --> 01:05:12,621
Wait a minute.

773
01:05:14,833 --> 01:05:17,876
We're going back to where we started.

774
01:05:18,967 --> 01:05:20,169
That's right. Why?

775
01:05:21,220 --> 01:05:22,671
We need to pick up my sister.

776
01:05:22,721 --> 01:05:25,884
But now we can get out with the vaccine.

777
01:05:26,225 --> 01:05:27,386
Oh, that's right.

778
01:05:27,636 --> 01:05:30,018
This way, there's an elevator to the roof.

779
01:05:30,179 --> 01:05:31,850
What's going on?

780
01:05:31,930 --> 01:05:32,868
SECURITY

781
01:05:32,892 --> 01:05:34,893
What are you suggesting here?

782
01:05:34,933 --> 01:05:37,066
But now we just need to go up.

783
01:05:37,106 --> 01:05:38,906
You expect us to go back to the control room?

784
01:06:14,273 --> 01:06:16,935
Control Room.

785
01:06:32,541 --> 01:06:33,622
What the hell?

786
01:06:33,662 --> 01:06:34,453
Hey!

787
01:06:34,663 --> 01:06:36,625
What do you think you're doing?

788
01:06:37,126 --> 01:06:38,127
You... What?

789
01:06:38,167 --> 01:06:39,128
What did you do?

790
01:06:39,168 --> 01:06:40,209
Stop it.

791
01:06:40,379 --> 01:06:42,091
Make it fucking stop!

792
01:06:44,093 --> 01:06:45,504
I can't let this bastard go.

793
01:06:45,554 --> 01:06:48,507
I'm taking him with me. You, follow me!

794
01:06:49,388 --> 01:06:50,389
Come on!

795
01:06:50,639 --> 01:06:52,101
What are you doing?

796
01:06:52,221 --> 01:06:53,512
Are you crazy?

797
01:06:54,183 --> 01:06:55,854
Don't touch that vaccine!

798
01:06:59,188 --> 01:07:02,401
I'm sorry, but give up on your sister.

799
01:07:03,232 --> 01:07:04,232
It's too late.

800
01:07:34,973 --> 01:07:37,146
Hyun-seok.

801
01:07:40,689 --> 01:07:42,441
Until he brings back his sister,

802
01:07:42,521 --> 01:07:43,902
we're going to wait here.

803
01:07:43,942 --> 01:07:45,154
Got it?

804
01:07:59,248 --> 01:08:00,669
Everyone listen up.

805
01:08:00,829 --> 01:08:04,213
This vaccine here is more important than anyone.

806
01:08:04,633 --> 01:08:06,675
This is for the whole world, okay?

807
01:08:11,840 --> 01:08:15,184
If you want to live, lead the way.

808
01:08:16,305 --> 01:08:17,476
Now!

809
01:08:32,030 --> 01:08:33,282
Hyun-seok!

810
01:08:33,532 --> 01:08:35,930
Are you okay? I'm going to you now.

811
01:08:35,954 --> 01:08:38,707
Which way is safe to go?

812
01:08:40,869 --> 01:08:42,621
Which way should I go?

813
01:08:43,622 --> 01:08:44,963
Hyun-hee!

814
01:08:47,296 --> 01:08:47,676
Um...

815
01:08:48,217 --> 01:08:50,379
Keep going straight ahead,

816
01:08:50,429 --> 01:08:51,880
and turn right.

817
01:08:54,933 --> 01:08:56,014
Okay, then what?

818
01:08:57,686 --> 01:08:59,478
This time, go left.

819
01:09:04,563 --> 01:09:06,485
Go straight, then take the stairs on the right.

820
01:09:06,645 --> 01:09:08,447
No no, stairs on the left!

821
01:09:08,567 --> 01:09:09,488
The left?

822
01:09:09,568 --> 01:09:10,465
Here? Is this right?

823
01:09:10,489 --> 01:09:11,177
Yeah.

824
01:09:11,201 --> 01:09:12,741
Go up those.

825
01:09:14,783 --> 01:09:16,115
Okay, I'm here.

826
01:09:16,365 --> 01:09:18,497
Go out the door and take the elevator.

827
01:09:18,537 --> 01:09:20,329
Here it is!

828
01:09:20,909 --> 01:09:21,976
I'm here!

829
01:09:22,000 --> 01:09:23,252
Are you okay?

830
01:09:27,216 --> 01:09:28,877
Hyun-hee, you made a mistake,

831
01:09:28,917 --> 01:09:31,470
this elevator doesn't go to the basement.

832
01:09:31,800 --> 01:09:33,762
You're all set now. Press the 4th floor.

833
01:09:34,383 --> 01:09:36,531
The 4th floor? Get off there?

